    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But that's just it, isn't it? The \"light\" you're talking about just feels like more noise. More obligations. More pretending that this weight isn't real. In the stories I read, the most beautiful things aren't the ones that fight to stay, but the ones that know when to let go. There's a certain dignity in a slow, quiet surrender to the shadows. It feels less like a tragedy and more like a natural conclusion. Like the house finally being allowed to sleep.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
