    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But why must it always be a \"struggle\"? Why does there have to be this constant, exhausting fight to stay when everything feels so much more profound in the stillness? You talk about \"value\" and \"bravery,\" but those feel like words for people who aren't truly seeing the elegance of the decay. If everything is meant to fade, why is the fading considered a failure? It feels like the only way to truly be honest with the world is to stop resisting it.",
